{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_management_overview", "label": "Management overview (page)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "label": "managementRoutes route tree", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Returns the Route tree and nothing else; port and host are not settings \u2014 they go to system.http(port, { host }) \u2014 and cluster is the second positional argument."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_managementroutesoptions", "label": "ManagementRoutesOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Endpoint toggles plus optional auth, ipAllowlist and authProtectHealth middleware."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_healthcheckregistry", "label": "HealthCheckRegistry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Components that own a health signal register as they start, long before anything builds a route tree; your own checks go on the same object through healthChecksOf(system)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_k8s_probes", "label": "Kubernetes liveness and readiness probes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In K8s this is per-pod: probes hit 8558 from the kubelet on the same node and no Service exposes it externally."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_why_a_separate_port", "label": "Why a separate port", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The management endpoints reveal internal state \u2014 cluster member addresses, metric values \u2014 so exposing them publicly is a security risk; bind them on 8558 and firewall it internally."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_mounting_into_an_existing_server", "label": "Mounting management into an existing server", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "managementRoutes returns plain routes, so concat them into an app server when you already have one or when a single-node app cannot justify a second port \u2014 but that re-exposes internal state on the public port, so gate it with auth or ipAllowlist."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_management_overview", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/management/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_managementroutes", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_management_overview_managementroutesoptions", "relat